l information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Contractions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You often \"contract\" or shorten words in English in conversation.<br/>Example: <span class = \"italic\">She is/She's, It is/It's</span><br/><br/>You  place an apostrophe (') in place of the missing letter or letters in writing."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Who's singing? (Who is singing?)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They're coming. (They are coming.)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Contraction\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She is<br/> She is not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She's <br/> She isn't / She's not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is <br/> He is not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He's<br/> He isn't / He's not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is<br/> It is not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's<br/> It isn't / It's not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They are <br/> They are not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They're<br/> They aren't\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le05ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Spain "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a Spanish speaking country in Europe "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a famous festival in Spain."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about a festival."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tomato   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a round, soft, red fruit that is eaten raw or cooked "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tomatoes are nice in salads."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strange "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "bizarre or unusual "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a place where strange things happen."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to celebrate  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do something special or enjoyable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The people in the village celebrate the festival every year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stain "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a mark on something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The tomato left a stain on my shirt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "patron saint "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a saint who protects a place or type of person "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The people of Bu\u00f1ol celebrated their patron saint, Luis Beltran."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The AY Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are some patterns that can help you identify  vowel sounds like the ay sound. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">A-E Words</span></br> You can add an -e to to the end of a word like mad to make <span class = \"italic\"> made</span>. Examples: cake, make, lake, fake"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">AI Words</span></br> You can use ai to make the AY (or long A) sound. Examples: strain, pain, main, gain"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">EI Words</span></br>You can use ei to make the AY (or long A) sound. Example: vein, eight, weight, beige"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We are going to pray in the church."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I made a tomato salad for lunch."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have a large stain on my shirt."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I can meet you at eight o'clock."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Say the words in the table aloud with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you do not know a word, look it up in a dictionary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 5 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make 5 sentences using one word from the table in each sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose as many words as you can to make a Tongue Twister.<br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\">The display was always onthe way to the subway.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Say your Tongue Twister to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I say words with the <span class=\"italic\">ay</span> sound to practice my pronunciation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make and practice a Tongue Twister."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I locate words in the dictionary to learn new words and practice saying them aloud."}]}], "type": "sena"}